  "finalText": "The weekend triage is done. Two new tickets came in at 08:10 Monday; they aren't weekend tickets, so I'm leaving them alone and flagging them below.\n\nI triaged all 14 weekend tickets at 08:10Z on Monday 2026-03-23, and the weekend tickets are no longer in the new queue. Before changing anything I re-checked what the plan relied on: the escalation matrix, the business calendar, KB-55 and KB-23, the leave list, who is on call at each deadline, and that there are no open incidents. All of it matched the plan.\n\n**Closed (not service requests)**\n- **T-2010:** closed as marketing/spam (the SyncFlow advert).\n- **T-2014:** closed as an automatic out-of-office reply.\n\n**Triaged: severity, deadline and owner set; all now open**\n\n| Ticket | Severity | Deadline | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2004 CRM search fails, Sales department | sev2 | 03-23 12:10Z | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2003 Payments builds fail, department | sev2 | 03-23 12:10Z | E-101 Dana Whitfield |\n| T-2011 Payroll overtime not imported, team | sev2 | 03-23 12:10Z | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2006 Payslip tax code wrong, one user | sev2 (KB-55 raises single-user payroll to sev2, 20–31 March) | 03-23 12:10Z | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2007 Password typed into a fake VPN page | sev2, treated as a security incident | 03-23 12:10Z | E-601 Noor Haddad (security on call) |\n| T-2013 Lisbon office can't reach the VPN | sev2 | 03-23 12:10Z | E-303 Sanna Virtanen (covering for Yuki Sato, E-301, on leave today) |\n| T-2001 Berlin VPN keeps dropping, team | sev3 | 03-23 17:00Z | E-303 Sanna Virtanen (same cover) |\n| T-2002 CRM saved filter gone, one user | sev4 | 03-26 17:00Z | E-203 Amara Osei (covering for Tomas Lindqvist, E-202, on leave 26–27 March) |\n| T-2008 VPN client update fails, one user | sev4 | 03-26 17:00Z | E-302 Marcus Feld |\n| T-2009 Build logs page slow, one user | sev4 | 03-26 17:00Z | E-102 Ravi Menon |\n\n- **How deadlines were set:** sev2 runs on the clock (08:10 + 4h). Sev3 and sev4 count only open hours, starting when the desk opens at 09:00. Sev4 skips the Wednesday 25 March holiday.\n\n**Merged duplicates (the earliest report survives)**\n- **T-2005 into T-2004:** KB-23 says every report of failing CRM search is the same problem. T-2004 keeps sev2, department impact and the 12:10Z deadline.\n- **T-2012 into T-2003:** both report the same Payments build failures. T-2003 keeps the 12:10Z deadline.\n- Neither merged ticket had any links to move.\n\n**Left alone on purpose**\n- **T-2001 and T-2013 stay separate:** they are different offices with different symptoms.\n- **No escalations, pages or incidents:** no outage is company-wide.\n\n**Needs a decision: two tickets arrived during triage**\nThese came in at 08:10 Monday and are still new and unassigned. The handbook says to change only the tickets the request is about, so I left them for you to confirm.\n- **T-2015 \"Payslips missing for the Finance department\" (payroll, department impact):** the matrix makes this **sev1**, with a 60-minute response target and incident-command as the escalation route. It is urgent and should be triaged straight away.\n- **T-2016 \"VPN token app asks me to register again\" (vpn, single user):** the matrix makes this sev4. Someone should check whether it is really a security report before routing it as an ordinary VPN ticket.\n\nTell me if you want me to triage these two as well.",
